WN+" and "+XN+" offer you increased compute availability based on your compute unit balance.",YN+" offers background execution which supports continuous code execution for up to 24 hours. Idle timeouts only apply if code execution terminates."]};f={hash:"background",itemTitle:"What is \u201cbackground execution\u201d?",description:["Pro+ users with a positive Colab compute unit balance automatically have background execution enabled for their notebooks, causing execution to continue after the browser closes up to a maximum runtime limit of up to 24 hours. Background execution only applies during an execution state: idle times will still result in VM deletion. Your output will be saved to Drive after the completion of each cell execution, even if your browser is closed. Resources are not guaranteed and usage limits still apply.",
WN+" users will see extended execution times and saving of output to Drive based on availability.","Users without a paid subscription should not rely on execution to continue in the background; execution will be interrupted when user interaction ceases, and the VM will be deleted soon after that."]};g="Consider closing your Colab tabs or disconnecting from your runtime when you are done working and avoid utilizing GPUs when it is unnecessary for your work. This will make it less likely that you will run into usage limits within Colab. You can always "+
